{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he saw.</b> Now, some said that the three men were one, and he is numerus [plural], and they are not separated. But they forgot \"and the two angels came to Sodom\" (Genesis 19:1). And the commentators said that HaShem appeared to him in visions of prophecy, and afterward he lifted his eyes and saw three angels — one to announce to Sarah, and the two went to Sodom: one to destroy and the second to save Lot." "And he interpreted \"and they ate\" as \"for the bread is eaten,\" like the sense of \"which the fire shall eat\" (Leviticus 6:3)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Reading נ' as numerus (Latin for 'grammatically plural'), following the common medieval Hebrew abbreviation; alternatively it may denote a specific plural form or grammatical term whose exact referent is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:55.207321484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}